#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:1
msgid "Architectural Update: Hardware Window, Wayland, and WebGPU"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:3
msgid "✨ New Wayland Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:5
msgid "Native Wayland Interactor (vtkWaylandRenderWindowInteractor):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:6
msgid ""
"A new, dedicated interactor has been implemented for robust event handling "
"on Wayland compositors. It processes pointer (mouse motion, buttons, "
"scrolling) and keyboard inputs directly, using xkbcommon for precise keymap "
"and modifier state management."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:11
msgid "Native Wayland Display Protocol Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:12
msgid ""
"This version introduces comprehensive, native support for the Wayland "
"display protocol, providing a modern alternative to X11 on Linux systems. "
"Windows can request standard decorations (title bars, borders) from the "
"Wayland compositor by leveraging the xdg-decoration-unstable-v1 protocol. "
"This ensures applications integrate visually with the user's desktop "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:18
msgid "WebGPU on Wayland:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:19
msgid ""
"The WebGPU rendering backend is now fully integrated with Wayland surfaces, "
"allowing high-performance graphics in modern Linux environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:22
msgid "🚀 Platform-Specific Enhancements & WebGPU Integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:23
msgid ""
"Significant advancements have been made to standardize and enhance the "
"rendering experience across diverse operating systems, including Windows, "
"macOS, and Linux. Historically, VTK's rendering architecture has been "
"characterized by a tightly coupled integration between the windowing system "
"and the graphics stack. However, with the advent of modern graphics APIs, "
"such as WebGPU, which offer more sophisticated and explicit surface "
"descriptors, VTK now implements a clear logical separation between its "
"graphics system and the underlying windowing system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:32
msgid ""
"This architectural shift is embodied by the introduction of the new "
"`vtkHardwareWindow` class and its specialized sub-classes. These components "
"are meticulously designed to manage platform-specific window system "
"integrations, critically, without incorporating any direct calls to the "
"rendering layer. This distinct separation not only facilitates superior "
"management and independent evolution of these two crucial codebases but also "
"significantly streamlines the integration of future graphics and windowing "
"APIs, thereby enhancing flexibility and long-term maintainability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:42
msgid "Windows: Improved Interactor and Hardware Window Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:43
msgid ""
"The `vtkWin32RenderWindowInteractor` has been updated to seamlessly support "
"both the legacy OpenGL render window and the new vtkHardwareWindow "
"abstraction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:46
msgid ""
"The `vtkWin32HardwareWindow` also supports native Windows cursor shapes and "
"visibility controls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:49
msgid "Apple (macOS/Cocoa) WebGPU Rendering via Metal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:50
msgid ""
"The `vtkCocoaHardwareWindow` now utilizes the WebGPU API with the Metal "
"backend, bringing modern, high-performance rendering to macOS applications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:53
msgid ""
"The `vtkCocoaHardwareView` is set as the \"first responder,\" allowing it to "
"properly intercept and process system keyboard and mouse events for reliable "
"interaction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:57
msgid "Linux (X11)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:58
msgid ""
"Unified Hardware Window: The specialized `vtkXWebGPURenderWindow` has been "
"removed in favor of the more generic `vtkXlibHardwareWindow`. This "
"simplifies the architecture by using a single, unified component for X11-"
"based windowing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:62
msgid "🔧 Refactoring & Build System Improvements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:64
msgid "Consolidated Win32 Build Logic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:65
msgid ""
"A new `VTK_USE_WIN32` CMake option has been introduced to replace disparate "
"WIN32 checks as well as the opengl dependent variable "
"`VTK_USE_WIN32_OPENGL`. This unifies conditional compilation and linking for "
"all Win32 components, simplifying the build configuration for Windows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:70
msgid "CMake Support for Wayland"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:71
msgid ""
"With the introduction of `FindWAYLAND.cmake` CMake script, the build system "
"finds and links against required Wayland libraries and generates necessary "
"protocol files, making it straightforward to build with Wayland support "
"enabled. To enable Wayland support, set `VTK_USE_Wayland:BOOL=ON`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:76
msgid "🐛 Bug Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:78
msgid "Fixed Xlib Macro Collision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/hardware-windows-and-wayland.md:79
msgid ""
"Resolved a critical compilation error on Linux systems where the Xlib "
"Success macro conflicted with the wgpu::MapAsyncStatus::Success enum, "
"allowing WebGPU code to build correctly with X11 headers. (Commit d8a4c55)"
msgstr ""
